        "Verify the root by testing interval endpoints $[1.275, 1.285]$ in $f(x) = 2x^3 - 5x^2 + 4$:\n$$f(1.275) = 2(1.275)^3 - 5(1.275)^2 + 4 = 4.14534 - 8.12813 + 4 = +0.0172 > 0$$\n$$f(1.285) = 2(1.285)^3 - 5(1.285)^2 + 4 = 4.24364 - 8.25613 + 4 = -0.0125 < 0$$\nThe change of sign confirms that the root lies in $[1.275, 1.285]$.",
